        <h2>Not Medical or Psychological Advice</h2>
        <p>Behavioral Psychology is an independent educational publication. Its articles explain concepts, theories, degree programs, and careers in behavioral psychology. They are written to inform, not to treat. Nothing on this site creates a therapist-patient, doctor-patient, or counselor-client relationship between you and the author.</p>

        <h2>Not a Clinician</h2>
        <p>The author, Hassam Shabbir, is a psychologist by training and a writer and author by profession. He is not a licensed clinician, and he does not practice therapy or counseling through this site. Articles about behavior change, habits, or conditioning describe general principles from the research literature. They are not instructions for self-treatment and should never be used as a substitute for professional care.</p>

        <h2>No Diagnosis or Treatment</h2>
        <p>Do not use anything you read here to diagnose yourself or anyone else, to decide whether to start or stop a medication, or to choose a course of treatment. If you have questions about a mental health condition, a behavioral concern, or any symptoms you are experiencing, speak with a qualified, licensed professional in your area.</p>

        <h2>If You Need Help Now</h2>
        <p>If you are in crisis or thinking about harming yourself, reach out right away. In the United States, you can call or text <strong>988</strong> to reach the 988 Suicide and Crisis Lifeline, available 24 hours a day, 7 days a week. You can also text <strong>HOME to 741741</strong> to reach the Crisis Text Line. Both services are free and confidential. If there is an immediate danger to life, call emergency services at <strong>911</strong>.</p>

        <h2>Accuracy and Currency</h2>
        <p>Articles are researched from reputable sources and reviewed before publication. Even so, the science of behavior evolves, and details such as statistics, program requirements, and professional standards change over time. The site does not guarantee that every page is complete, current, or free of error. Always verify important details with the primary source, and consult qualified professionals before making health, education, or career decisions based on what you read here.</p>

        <h2>External Links</h2>
        <p>Articles link to outside sources for reference and further reading. The site does not control those sources and is not responsible for their content or accuracy.</p>

        <p><em>Last updated: November 2026. Questions about this disclaimer can be sent to <a href="mailto:info@behavioralpsychology.pro">info@behavioralpsychology.pro</a>.</em></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
